{"1-5":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0995","lemma":"בִּין","tr":"bin","gloss":"to understand","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":170},{"base":"H8451","lemma":"תּוֹרָה","tr":"to·rah","gloss":"instruction","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":219},{"base":"H7563","lemma":"רָשָׁע","tr":"ra·sah","gloss":"wicked","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":263},{"base":"H5502","lemma":"סָחַף","tr":"sa·chaph","gloss":"to prostatrate","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H0369","lemma":"אַ֫יִן","tr":"a·yin","gloss":"nothing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":788},{"base":"H1624","lemma":"גָּרָה","tr":"ga·rah","gloss":"to stir up","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H7326","lemma":"רוּשׁ","tr":"rush","gloss":"be poor","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H3715","lemma":"כְּפִיר","tr":"ke·phir","gloss":"lion","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":32},{"base":"H0748","lemma":"אָרַךְ","tr":"a·rakh","gloss":"to prolong","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":34},{"base":"H6231","lemma":"עָשַׁק","tr":"a·shaq","gloss":"to oppress","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":36}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":28,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":147,"source":"both","text":"The LORD will cause the enemies who rise up against you to be defeated before you. They will march out against you in one direction but flee from you in seven.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":53,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":90,"source":"both","text":"There they are, overwhelmed with dread, where there was nothing to fear. For God has scattered the bones of those who besieged you. You put them to shame, for God has despised them.","from":1},{"book":"ISA","chapter":26,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":74,"source":"openbible","text":"You will keep in perfect peace the steadfast of mind, because he trusts in You.","from":1},{"book":"ISA","chapter":26,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":74,"source":"openbible","text":"Trust in the LORD forever, because GOD the LORD is the Rock eternal.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":27,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":71,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD is my light and my salvation— whom shall I fear? The LORD is the stronghold of my life— whom shall I dread?","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":27,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":71,"source":"openbible","text":"When the wicked came upon me to devour my flesh, my enemies and foes stumbled and fell.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":112,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":56,"source":"both","text":"He does not fear bad news; his heart is steadfast, trusting in the LORD.","from":1},{"book":"1TH","chapter":2,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":44,"source":"both","text":"As you are aware, we had already endured suffering and shameful treatment in Philippi. But in the face of strong opposition, we were bold in our God to speak to you the gospel of God.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"6-11":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H6223","lemma":"עָשִׁיר","tr":"a·shir","gloss":"rich","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":23},{"base":"H1800","lemma":"דַּל","tr":"dal","gloss":"poor","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":47},{"base":"H0995","lemma":"בִּין","tr":"bin","gloss":"to understand","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":170},{"base":"H8451","lemma":"תּוֹרָה","tr":"to·rah","gloss":"instruction","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":219},{"base":"H2896","lemma":"טוֹב","tr":"tov","gloss":"pleasant","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":538},{"base":"H8636","lemma":"תַּרְבִּית","tr":"tar·bit","gloss":"increment","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H2151","lemma":"זָלַל","tr":"za·lal","gloss":"to shake","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H1870","lemma":"דֶּ֫רֶךְ","tr":"de·rekh","gloss":"way: conduct","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":706},{"base":"H6141","lemma":"עִקֵּשׁ","tr":"iq·qesh","gloss":"twisted","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H5392","lemma":"נֶ֫שֶׁךְ","tr":"ne·shekh","gloss":"interest","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":66,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"If I had cherished iniquity in my heart, the Lord would not have listened.","from":9},{"book":"2TI","chapter":4,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"For the time will come when men will not tolerate sound doctrine, but with itching ears they will gather around themselves teachers to suit their own desires.","from":9},{"book":"2TI","chapter":4,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"So they will turn their ears away from the truth and turn aside to myths.","from":9},{"book":"ISA","chapter":1,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"When you spread out your hands in prayer, I will hide My eyes from you; even though you multiply your prayers, I will not listen. Your hands are covered with blood.","from":9},{"book":"ISA","chapter":1,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"Wash and cleanse yourselves. Remove your evil deeds from My sight. Stop doing evil!","from":9},{"book":"ZEC","chapter":7,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"But they refused to pay attention and turned a stubborn shoulder; they stopped up their ears from hearing.","from":9},{"book":"ZEC","chapter":7,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"And just as I had called and they would not listen, so when they called I would not listen, says the LORD of Hosts.","from":9},{"book":"PSA","chapter":109,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"When he is tried, let him be found guilty, and may his prayer be regarded as sin.","from":9}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"12-16":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H7563","lemma":"רָשָׁע","tr":"ra·sah","gloss":"wicked","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":263},{"base":"H4642","lemma":"מַעֲשַׁקָּה","tr":"ma·a·shaq·qah","gloss":"oppression","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H7227","lemma":"רַב","tr":"rav","gloss":"many","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":454},{"base":"H5098","lemma":"נָהַם","tr":"na·ham","gloss":"to groan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H0120","lemma":"אָדָם","tr":"a·dam","gloss":"man","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":550},{"base":"H8264","lemma":"שָׁקַק","tr":"sha·qaq","gloss":"to rush","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H5970","lemma":"עָלַץ","tr":"a·lats","gloss":"to rejoice","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H1677","lemma":"דֹּב","tr":"dov","gloss":"bear","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H2638","lemma":"חָסֵר","tr":"cha·ser","gloss":"lacking","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H1215","lemma":"בֶּ֫צַע","tr":"be·tsa","gloss":"unjust-gain","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1JN","chapter":1,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":44,"source":"openbible","text":"If we say we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us.","from":13},{"book":"1JN","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":44,"source":"openbible","text":"If we say we have not sinned, we make Him out to be a liar, and His word is not in us.","from":13},{"book":"PSA","chapter":32,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":38,"source":"openbible","text":"When I kept silent, my bones became brittle from my groaning all day long.","from":13},{"book":"PSA","chapter":32,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":38,"source":"openbible","text":"Then I acknowledged my sin to You and did not hide my iniquity. I said, “I will confess my transgressions to the LORD,” and You forgave the guilt of my sin. Selah","from":13},{"book":"JOB","chapter":31,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"if I have covered my transgressions like Adam by hiding my guilt in my heart,","from":13},{"book":"LUK","chapter":15,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"I will get up and go back to my father and say to him, “Father, I have sinned against heaven and against you.","from":13},{"book":"LUK","chapter":15,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"For this son of mine was dead and is alive again! He was lost and is found!’ So they began to celebrate.","from":13},{"book":"PRO","chapter":23,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"Do not let your heart envy sinners, but always continue in the fear of the LORD.","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"17-22":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H7646","lemma":"שָׂבֵעַ","tr":"sa·va","gloss":"to satisfy","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":97},{"base":"H3899","lemma":"לֶ֫חֶם","tr":"le·chem","gloss":"food","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":298},{"base":"H2639","lemma":"חֶ֫סֶר","tr":"che·ser","gloss":"poverty","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6140","lemma":"עָקַשׁ","tr":"a·qash","gloss":"to twist","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H7389","lemma":"רֵישׁ","tr":"resh","gloss":"poverty","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H0213","lemma":"אוּץ","tr":"uts","gloss":"to hasten","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H7386","lemma":"רֵיק","tr":"req","gloss":"worthless","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H6595","lemma":"פַּת","tr":"pat","gloss":"morsel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"H6238","lemma":"עָשַׁר","tr":"a·shar","gloss":"to enrich","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H8551","lemma":"תָּמַךְ","tr":"ta·makh","gloss":"to grasp","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LUK","chapter":16,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"Whoever is faithful with very little will also be faithful with much, and whoever is dishonest with very little will also be dishonest with much.","from":20},{"book":"LUK","chapter":16,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"And if you have not been faithful with the belongings of another, who will give you belongings of your own?","from":20},{"book":"PRO","chapter":10,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"He who walks in integrity walks securely, but he who perverts his ways will be found out.","from":18},{"book":"PRO","chapter":13,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Dishonest wealth will dwindle, but what is earned through hard work will be multiplied.","from":20},{"book":"PRO","chapter":28,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Better a poor man who walks with integrity than a rich man whose ways are perverse.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Whoever sheds the blood of man, by man his blood will be shed; for in His own image God has made mankind.","from":17},{"book":"PRO","chapter":12,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The one who works his land will have plenty of food, but whoever chases fantasies lacks judgment.","from":19},{"book":"PRO","chapter":18,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Showing partiality to the wicked is not good, nor is depriving the innocent of justice.","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"23-28":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0982","lemma":"בָּטַח","tr":"ba·tach","gloss":"to trust","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":120},{"base":"H3994","lemma":"מְאֵרָה","tr":"me·e·rah","gloss":"curse","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H0120","lemma":"אָדָם","tr":"a·dam","gloss":"man","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":550},{"base":"H4066","lemma":"מָדוֹן","tr":"ma·don","gloss":"strife","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H0369","lemma":"אַ֫יִן","tr":"a·yin","gloss":"nothing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":788},{"base":"H1878","lemma":"דָּשֵׁן","tr":"da·shen","gloss":"to prosper","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H2270","lemma":"חָבֵר","tr":"cha·ver","gloss":"companion","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H4270","lemma":"מַחְסוֹר","tr":"mach·sor","gloss":"need","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H1624","lemma":"גָּרָה","tr":"ga·rah","gloss":"to stir up","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H7342","lemma":"רָחָב","tr":"ra·chav","gloss":"Broad","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":3,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":27,"source":"both","text":"Trust in the LORD with all your heart, and lean not on your own understanding;","from":26},{"book":"JER","chapter":17,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"The heart is deceitful above all things and beyond cure. Who can understand it?","from":26},{"book":"JOB","chapter":28,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"And He said to man, ‘Behold, the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom, and to turn away from evil is understanding.’”","from":26},{"book":"PRO","chapter":19,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"Kindness to the poor is a loan to the LORD, and He will repay the lender.","from":27},{"book":"PRO","chapter":27,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Better an open rebuke than love that is concealed.","from":23},{"book":"PRO","chapter":27,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"The wounds of a friend are faithful, but the kisses of an enemy are deceitful.","from":23},{"book":"PRO","chapter":29,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"When the righteous flourish, the people rejoice, but when the wicked rule, the people groan.","from":28},{"book":"JOB","chapter":24,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"They push the needy off the road and force all the poor of the land into hiding.","from":28}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}